WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:02.610
- [Narrator] The Bank of
England may have been busy

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.220
printing money with King
Charles III's face on it,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.650
but little is known about
how much money he makes

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.510
or how much he's worth.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.030
He's inherited land,
properties and other items

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.710
from Queen Elizabeth II,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:18.450
and one estimate suggests his
fortune is some $745 million.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.700
But a lack of transparency from the royals

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.810
makes it difficult to determine
exactly how rich Charles is.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.270
Here's what we do know
about his sources of income

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.620
and what it all adds up to.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.260
Charles has always had

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.510
something of an entrepreneurial spirit.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.570
In 1990, he launched his
Duchy Originals range

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.160
of organic oat biscuits,

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.930
which later expanded to other products

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.790
made on the prince's estate.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.200
Those products were eventually sold

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.810
exclusively in British
supermarket Waitrose

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.310
as part of a partnership deal.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.900
The brand reported profits
of over $4 million last year,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.040
all of which was donated

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.390
to the Prince of Wales's
charitable foundation.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.200
As the Prince of Wales
and heir to the throne

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.540
Charles also controlled
the Duchy of Cornwall,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.870
an estate with net assets of 1.3 billion,

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:08.730
which covers almost 130,000
acres of land across England.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:13.380
Its net assets have increased
in value by 44% since 2012,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.240
with Charles seeing his
income from the estate

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.540
increase 25% over the past decade.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.200
He raked in $28.3 million
last year, mostly through rent

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.110
from commercial and
residential properties.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.330
Now that Charles is king,
the Duchy of Cornwall,

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.400
along with its multimillion dollar income,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.260
goes to his eldest son, William.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.350
- He succeeds me as Duke of Cornwall

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.730
and takes on the responsibilities
for the Duchy of Cornwall

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.753
which I have undertaken
for more than five decades.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.860
- [Narrator] But that hardly
leaves the king destitute.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.710
Charles inherited the Duchy
of Lancaster from his mother,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.900
worth around $800 million.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.450
It consists of more than 45,000 acres

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.880
of commercial, agricultural
and residential properties

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.110
in England and Wales

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.360
and provides a private
income for the monarch.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.800
The late queen earned $29.7
million from it last year,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.120
and there's nothing to suggest

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.400
her son won't take home a similar amount.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.760
He also doesn't have to pay
any taxes on Duchy revenue,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.830
though he will follow
in the queen's footsteps

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.630
and opt to pay income tax

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.900
after deducting money
spent on official duties.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.190
But the Duchy of Lancaster

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.380
isn't the monarch's only source of income,

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.883
or even their most valuable.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.970
A large amount of King Charles's income

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.370
derives from something
called the Sovereign Grant.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.690
Here's how that works.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.300
In the 1700s, the monarchy
handed over revenues

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.130
from swaths of land to the government

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.020
known as the Crown Estate.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.670
These days, the Crown Estate makes money

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.880
on a range of assets from
retail property to golf courses

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.040
and even offshore wind farms.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.040
Those assets are valued
at around $20 billion.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.700
- I take this opportunity
to continue the tradition

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.550
of surrendering the hereditary revenues,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.560
including the Crown Estate,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.890
to my government for the benefit of all

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.920
in return for the Sovereign Grant.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.120
- [Narrator] Every year
the government pays

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.640
a percentage of the profits
made on those assets

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.990
back to the monarchy.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.843
Last year, it totaled
more than $106 million.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.440
That was used to fund the
queen's official duties

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.710
and maintain royal residencies,
including Buckingham Palace,

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.990
which is kept in a trust
for the reigning monarch.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.210
The king does not personally
own the properties

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.410
making up the Crown Estate

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.170
and can't sell them for
his own financial gain,

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.520
unlike the two properties

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.350
we know he inherited from his mother,

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.760
Sandringham House in Norfolk

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.710
and Balmoral Castle in Scotland

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.233
which has been in the
royal family since 1852.

00:03:35.155 --> 00:03:36.570
- [Reporter] The 80,000 acre preserve

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.590
in the Scottish Highlands

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.510
has since been the holiday retreat

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.282
for Britain's ruling families.

00:03:41.282 --> 00:03:43.782
(happy music)

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.660
- [Narrator] The two estates passed

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.620
from monarch to monarch

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.950
until Edward VIII's abdication in 1936

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.150
when a financial settlement

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.920
saw them transferred to his brother

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.720
and Charles's grandfather George VI.

00:03:55.762 --> 00:03:58.950
Each is valued between $66 and $79 million

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.420
by one royal expert,

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.330
although a potential market
price for this kind of asset

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.980
is difficult to determine.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.960
Last year, a cottage on
the Sandringham Estate

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.910
was made available on Airbnb

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.190
as a holiday rental by Norfolk Hideaways.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.780
Visitors can book the Garden House

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:15.570
for just over $1,000 per night.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:16.920
Norfolk Hideaways couldn't say

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.050
how much of any revenue from the listing

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.910
went back to the royal family.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.910
The Balmoral Estate in Scotland
also rents out cottages

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.340
in addition to selling ticketed tours.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.810
The king could also have inherited

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.570
Queen Elizabeth's personal
investment portfolio,

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.330
the value of which is undisclosed.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.460
The palace won't comment
on the monarch's wealth

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.080
or the contents of wills.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.940
They say it's a private matter.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.670
We do know that Charles
paid no inheritance tax

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.460
on any of the assets
passed to him by the queen.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.350
But unlike other UK citizens,

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.620
royal family members don't have
to make their wills public.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.000
This means we can't determine

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.800
what Charles inherited from his mother

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.360
or father Prince Philip,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.853
so we may never know
what he's truly worth.

